From: spike #23 (LilOS engine-hermes spike)
Subject: [PATCH] tui_gateway: accept mcp_servers on session.create

Proposal ONLY — do not open upstream without the maintainers' ack. Mirrors
what ACP `session/new {mcpServers}` already does in
`acp_adapter/server.py::_register_session_mcp_servers` (runtime
`register_mcp_servers` + per-agent `mcp-<name>` toolset expansion), but for
the WS/stdio `session.create` path so a host can scope an MCP server to ONE
session instead of the whole profile.

Wire shape mirrors ACP `McpServerStdio | McpServerHttp | McpServerSse`:
stdio `{name, command, args?, env?}`; remote `{name, url, headers?}`.

Key design points:
- `SessionCreateParams` gains `mcp_servers` (extra=forbid, so it must be
  declared); entries validate into the same config dict shape
  `register_mcp_servers` consumes (see `acp_adapter/server.py::_mcp_server_config`).
- The list is stored on the session record (`session["session_mcp_servers"]`)
  at create; NOT written to profile config — config writes stay with
  `mcp.servers.add` / `profiles.configure`.
- At agent build (`_make_agent`), after `_load_enabled_toolsets(platform)`
  resolves the profile surface, the session's servers are registered into
  the session's profile scope (existing `_mcp_registry_scope()` /
  `register_mcp_servers` machinery — identical to the ACP path) and
  `mcp-<name>` toolset names are appended to this agent's
  `enabled_toolsets`. Other sessions of the same profile never see them:
  `enabled_mcp_server_names` reads config+plugins only.
- Trust: session-supplied servers inherit the calling profile's
  `mcp_servers.<name>.trust` policy when the name matches a configured
  server; unknown names default to `untrusted` (write-capable calls then
  require approval via `_trust_gate_check`).
- Resume/load parity would need the same field on SessionResumeParams;
  left out here since persisted session rows can't safely replay an MCP
  client-supplied command on resume without re-prompting (server binaries
  may have changed). Hosts should re-send `mcp_servers` on `session.resume`
  if we extend this.

diff --git a/tui_gateway/contracts/sessions.py b/tui_gateway/contracts/sessions.py
--- a/tui_gateway/contracts/sessions.py
+++ b/tui_gateway/contracts/sessions.py
@@ class SessionCreateParams(ProfileParams):
     close_on_disconnect: bool = False
     hidden: bool = False
     room_plumbing: bool = False
     follow_profile_config: bool = False
+    # Session-scoped MCP servers (ACP session/new parity): register at
+    # create time and expose only to this session's agent via mcp-<name>
+    # toolsets. Never persisted to profile config.
+    mcp_servers: list[dict] | None = None

diff --git a/tui_gateway/methods_session.py b/tui_gateway/methods_session.py
@@ def _create_session(...):
     ...
+    # Stash on the deferred session record; consumed by _make_agent (server.py).
+    session_mcp_servers = params.get("mcp_servers") or None
@@
     ... _deferred_session_record(..., session_mcp_servers=session_mcp_servers, ...)

diff --git a/tui_gateway/server.py b/tui_gateway/server.py
@@ def _init_session(...):
     "profile_home": profile_home,
+    "session_mcp_servers": <from create params>,
@@ def _make_agent(...):
     platform = _resolve_agent_platform(platform_override)
+    session = _sessions.get(sid)  # already done below; reuse
+    session_mcp = (session or {}).get("session_mcp_servers")
+    if session_mcp:
+        # Same mechanism as acp_adapter/server.py::_register_session_mcp_servers:
+        # runtime registration keyed to the session's profile scope (no config
+        # write), then this agent's toolsets gain mcp-<name> only.
+        try:
+            from tools.mcp_tool_discovery import register_mcp_servers
+            configs = {s["name"]: _session_mcp_config(s) for s in session_mcp}
+            register_mcp_servers(configs)   # scope = session profile_home (bound by caller)
+            extra_toolsets = [f"mcp-{s['name']}" for s in session_mcp if s.get("name")]
+        except Exception:
+            logger.warning("session %s: session mcp_servers registration failed", sid, exc_info=True)
+            extra_toolsets = []
+    else:
+        extra_toolsets = []
     agent = AIAgent(
         ...
-        enabled_toolsets=_load_enabled_toolsets(platform),
+        enabled_toolsets=(_load_enabled_toolsets(platform) or []) + extra_toolsets or None,
         ...

+def _session_mcp_config(entry: dict) -> dict:
+    """ACP-style server entry -> config dict for register_mcp_servers.
+    Accepts stdio {name, command, args?, env?} and remote {name, url, headers?};
+    anything else is rejected (a session cannot silently widen trust/transport)."""
+    if entry.get("command"):
+        return {"command": entry["command"], "args": list(entry.get("args") or []),
+                "env": dict(entry.get("env") or {})}
+    if entry.get("url"):
+        return {"url": entry["url"], "headers": dict(entry.get("headers") or {})}
+    raise ValueError(f"mcp_servers entry {entry.get('name')!r} needs command or url")
